TIKI
// HZM coop [2026-09-05, bug-2477] THE RAMP-DROP HULL SPARK, on its own name.
//
// This is the ONE block of maintt/zzzzzzzz_hd_fxfix.pk3's models/fx/bh_metal_lite.tik that a
// script_model carrier actually renders. Every `sfx` block in that file - the originspawn sparks,
// the corona flash, both blockdlights, the volumetric smoke - is recorded only while the client
// special-effects manager is loading an effect (StartSFXCommand returns at once when
// m_pCurrentSfx is NULL), so on a carrier spawned from script they never existed; what runs per
// entity is CG_UpdateEntityEmitters over the `originemitter` blocks, of which that file has one.
//
// WHY IT IS COPIED AND WHAT CHANGED, measured in cg_tempmodels.cpp (the retail name cannot be
// overridden - hd_fxfix sorts last and wins it, the shader-isolation recipe, bug-922):
//   * `velocity 450` is the ONLY term that follows the carrier's ANGLES: forwardVelocity rides
//     vForward, captured from the emitter axis before the particle loop (the axis UpdateEmitter
//     copied from the entity). Everything else is world-space: the per-particle
//     AnglesToAxis(p->cgd.angles, ...) rebuilds the emitter axis from the block's own angles (zero
//     here) BEFORE randvelaxis reads it, so `notagaxis` changes nothing, and the tag axis is the
//     identity for a tagless emitter.
//   * `radialvelocity` was REMOVED: for a point emitter it reassigns the velocity to (origin -
//     start) = zero, wiping the forward term after it was applied - the retail block's own
//     commented-out `//velocity 453.00` is why its sparks always flew along world +X.
//   * `randvelaxis range 294 312 ...` became small world-space `randvel` jitter, so the burst
//     still scatters but no longer has a 300 u/s +X term in it.
// The result: coop_rampHullHit turns each carrier up and inboard and the sparks go where it faces.
setup
{
	scale 1.0
	path models/fx/dummy
	skelmodel dummy2.skd
}

init
{
	server
	{
	}
	client
	{
		cache models/fx/bh_metal_fastpiece.tik

		originemitter fountain
		(
			spawnrate 300.00
			model models/fx/bh_metal_fastpiece.tik
			color 1.00 1.00 1.00
			life .35
			velocity 450
			randvel range -40 80 range -40 80 range -12 24
			accel 0.00 0.00 -300.00
			avelocity crandom 5 crandom 5 crandom 5
			alignstretch 0.09
		)
	}
}

// This section is just needed to be a valid tiki file
animations
{
	idle dummy2.skc
}
